+        // at the receiver ± h on the cascade map, h = 0.5 * c[56].xy (UV) of their lighting block (fp_c9, or fp_c5 in
+        // some), the same in every cascade. In the near cascade the map is sharp enough that the four copies of an edge
+        // show apart. In a fragment shader that has a 2D array shadow sampler, reads of element 56 .x and .y from any
+        // constant buffer but fp_c4 (which holds the cascade matrices, row 56 being cascade 3's depth row) are multiplied
